C. WOULD AN OBSERVED SOLAR CYCLE HELP? -- ASKED OF THE OBSERVATIONS FIRST
==========================================================================
  1. THE SOLAR CYCLE'S TEMPERATURE SIGNATURE IS ALREADY IN THE MODEL.
     CCX is driven with the OBSERVED GMST record, which contains whatever
     the solar cycle did to temperature -- exactly the argument R/forcing.R
     :979-988 already makes for volcanic cooling. A solar -> temperature
     term would DOUBLE-COUNT. The only non-redundant addition would be a
     DIRECT irradiance -> photosynthesis path, the solar analogue of
     `gamma_diff` -- and that is a new mechanism, not a new forcing column.

  2. BEST-FITTING PERIOD in 9-13 yr: 9.4 yr, amplitude 0.477 GtC/yr
     = 52.4 % of the anomaly's sd (0.911), i.e. 13.7 % of its VARIANCE.
     WHITE-NOISE NULL over the same band: median 0.316, 95% 0.502
     ⇒ observed 0.477 sits at the 93th percentile of the null.
  3. FOR SCALE: closing gate V needs 0.343 (GtC/yr)^2 of extra variance;
     a harmonic of the observed amplitude carries 0.114, i.e. 33 % of it.
  4. POWER: the 95% null cut is 0.502 GtC/yr, so this test DETECTS any
     harmonic in the band above that amplitude -- 15 % of the observed
     variance -- and CANNOT rule out smaller ones. On 66 years (~6.0
     cycles) that is the honest statement: a solar cycle big enough to matter
     for gate V would have shown; one too small to matter might not have.

